xbrli:xbrl.in-capmkt:RelatedPartyTransactionExplana:
1. Transactions between JM Financial Limited (the "Company") and its Wholly Owned Subsidiaries are excluded. 
2. The disclosures include Related Party Transactions entered into by subsidiaries viz., JM Financial Products Limited and JM Financial Credit Solutions Limited, which ceased to be high value debt listed entities. The disclosures also include transactions entered into by their respective step-down subsidiaries, viz., JM Financial Home Loans Limited and JM Financial Asset Reconstruction Company Limited;
3. The amount shown in the "Value of transaction" column represents the aggregate value of all related party transactions entered into during the reporting period. The maximum value of such transactions at any point in time did not exceed the limit approved by the Company's Audit Committee and/or shareholders, as applicable;
4. The related party transactions reported above have been identified based on the Permanent Account Number (PAN) of each related party available on record;
5. Non-convertible debentures transactions include only primary issuances. Outstanding balances represent NCDs held by related parties as on reporting date;
6. The transaction is between two wholly owned subsidiaries of the Company, whose accounts are consolidated with those of the Company. Accordingly, prior approval of the Audit Committee of the Company is not required, pursuant to Regulation 23(5)(c )of the SEBI Listing Regulations;
7. The transaction has been entered into by a subsidiary of the Company, to which the Company is not a party, and its value, whether individually or taken together with previous transactions during the financial year, does not exceed the threshold specified under Regulation 23(2)(b) of the SEBI Listing Regulations. Accordingly, prior approval of the Audit Committee of the Company is not required; and
8. Rs. 0.00 denotes an amount below Rs. 50,000.
